H2: Known Faults - MINI Cooper
H3: Timing Chain and Guides
P: HIGH ú 2006-2013 ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says neglected R56 cars can use a fair bit of engine oil and, if run low, can wear out the chains and guides. It advises listening for rattles on initial cold starting and walking away if they are evident, as this is big, messy and expensive. Autocar says the Cooper S of 2007-13 likes to throw its timing chain, and that a brushing noise or perhaps a rattle from cold at idle comes as a few hints first. It says the problem is more likely on engines fitted before 2011, after which a revised chain tensioner was installed.
H3: Oil Consumption
P: MONITOR ú 2006-2024 ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says Cooper models of the 2006-2013 generation are often known for high oil consumption that can cause rapid turbocharger death. Autocar says the 2007-13 Cooper S engine likes a drink, as much as a litre of oil every 1000 miles. One Carbuyer owner of a 2006-2014 MINI hatchback says high oil consumption is something that should be noted. For the 2014-2024 hatch, Parkers says to expect every engine to consume some oil during use, so a full service history and quality engine oil are imperative.
H3: Water Pump and Thermostat
P: MONITOR ú 2006-2013 ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says that if a noise vanishes with a blip of the throttle, be cautious, as this normally is a sign of a worn water pump. It also says issues with the coolant sensor or thermostat can throw up an ECU warning light and cause a fuelling issue.
H3: Power Steering Pump
P: MONITOR ú 2006-2013 ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says lumpy, stiff or noisy electric power steering pumps have dogged the MINI for many years.
H3: Crankshaft Bearing on Cooper S
P: CHECK ú 2014-2015 ú Get a quote
P: Autocar says to be wary of Cooper S MINIs built between 2014 and 2015. A recall was issued to repair a defective crankshaft bearing, and engines were either rebuilt or replaced.
H3: Fuel Injectors
P: MONITOR ú 2014-2024 ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says fuel injectors on the 2014-2024 hatch can leak and even fail over time, which means they will need replacing.
H3: Oil Leaks and Brittle Plastics
P: CHECK ú 2001-2006 ú Get a quote
P: For the R50 of 2001-2006, Parkers says oil leaks from sump and cam cover gaskets are common, and plastic components, including the oil dipstick handle, can go brittle and break.
H3: Gearbox Jumping Out of Gear
P: CHECK ú 2001-2006 ú Get a quote
P: On the 2001-2006 R50, Parkers says any difficulty engaging gear, or jumping out of gear, should not be dismissed as just being a bit of wear.
H3: Electrical Faults and Infotainment
P: MINOR ú 2014-2024 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says most of the faults that did occur on the 2014-2024 MINI Hatchback were related to electrical components, including the infotainment system.
H3: Tired Shocks and Bushings on Cooper S JCW
P: MINOR ú 2008-2014 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says the Cooper S JCW's suspension can suffer from tired shocks and bushings if the car has been used enthusiastically. It calls the transmission tough, and the engine co-developed by PSA Peugeot Citroen and BMW a real standout, offering decent reliability and modest fuel consumption.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists these two MINI Cooper recalls.
LI: On affected vehicles the windscreen wiper wiring harness may be routed incorrectly and can be damaged by contact with the windscreen wiper mechanism.
LI: On affected vehicles the brake servomotor was improperly welded.
P: Enter the registration in our recall check to see whether a car has an open DVSA safety recall.
